      "summary": "A runtime where UI controls report semantic events and a Jev or mock policy picks which registered affordance to present.",
      "problem": "It replaces hard-wired interface flows: buttons describe what happened, the policy answers with a decision and confidence, and safety gates fall back instead of improvising.",
      "requirements_text": "The policy layer can run against Jev or a mock; the README does not state account or key requirements for the Jev path. Runs as a local prototype.",
